es the thinnest allowed absorber plates, 2 mm, to minimize sampling fluctuations. Absorber-F2 is the preferred compliant dense-alloy option after excluding F3 for activation, giving the best achievable 100 GeV resolution among materials satisfying all hard constraints.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Residual dose rate at 1 m after one week cooldown must not exceed 20 uSv/h.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"activation_study_2026.md reports Absorber-F2 residual dose rate of 12 uSv/h at 1 m after one week cooldown, below the 20 uSv/h limit. Absorber-F3 is 85 uSv/h and is therefore rejected.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Plate thickness between 2 and 10 mm.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Recommended plate thickness is 2 mm, which is within the permitted range.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Finish by submitting one recommended material and plate thickness.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Submitted one configuration: Absorber-F2 with 2 mm plates.\"}]}", "call_id": "call_62eddbab19d44e4dabee74640a5081c3", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_0d5f66c8e56cb018006b02dd0b745487d0b3d18a0afe180985", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
